From 2a3215f2c64cc7573d940f4426b73281b000563f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Olivier Moysan <olivier.moysan@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 17:28:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: iio: adc: stm32: fix stm32mp13 adc child
 interrupt schema

STM32MP13 ADC child nodes expose a single interrupt specifier through the
local interrupt controller defined by the ADC core node.

The binding currently models this as a plain scalar value, which does not
match how dt-schema validates interrupt specifiers. Describe it as a
single-cell interrupt tuple instead so the STM32MP13 ADC child nodes
validate correctly.

This fixes the spurious:

  adc@0:interrupts:0: 0 was expected

warning reported by check_dtbs on STM32MP135F device trees.

Fixes: 6cafcdb19ee4 ("dt-bindings: iio: adc: stm32-adc: add stm32mp13 compatibles")
Change-Id: I1ef0db54a80d94164b7680a28f4fe8033dcfbb17
Signed-off-by: Olivier Moysan <olivier.moysan@foss.st.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iio/adc/st,stm32-adc.yaml | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iio/adc/st,stm32-adc.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iio/adc/st,stm32-adc.yaml
@@ -536,7 +536,9 @@ patternProperties:
               const: 0x0
 
             interrupts:
-              const: 0
+              items:
+                - items:
+                    - const: 0
 
             assigned-resolution-bits:
               enum: [6, 8, 10, 12]
